  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>In the heart of Sainte-Maxime, one specific area of the town-centre beach, by the Pont du Préconil bridge, is the only part where dogs are allowed. The town itself calls it "the town-centre dog beach". The rest of Luc Provensal beach, facing due south towards Saint-Tropez, with its beach clubs and pine grove, remains closed to dogs.</p>

      <h2>Good to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to the Sainte-Maxime town hall and tourist office, two coastal areas are open to dogs all year: this area of the town-centre beach and the land part of <a href="/en/fiche-pointe-des-sardinaux-sainte-maxime">Pointe des Sardinaux</a>, except in July and August. Owners must keep their dog on a leash at all times and pick up after it, for the cleanliness of the sites and to get along with other users.</p>
      <p>Everywhere else, dogs are banned all year: the town-centre beach outside the authorised area, Les Oursins, La Nartelle and La Garonnette beaches, and the southern tip of Pointe des Sardinaux. The official page for Plage des Éléphants states "animals not accepted, kept on a leash", and the Luc Provensal beach page states that animals are only accepted in the area under the Pont du Préconil. Only guide and assistance dogs are allowed on all beaches, all year.</p>
      <p>The town-centre beach is free to access and open all year, with parking, toilets and beach restaurants nearby. The beach first-aid post operates from 12 June to 13 September 2026: the dog area is under the Pont du Préconil, so locate it on site before setting down your things.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: look for the signs by the Pont du Préconil before laying down your towel — the area is short and the neighbouring beaches remain banned.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>To let your dog run off the leash, the town created the Jardin des Chiens des Virgiles, behind the Virgiles school, close to the town centre: access along the school or via the footbridge on the motorhome parking side (Neuenbürg roundabout). Dogs roam freely there, except category 2 dogs, and must stay under their owners' constant supervision; the rules are available on the town hall website.</p>
      <p>The town has 130 dog-waste bag dispensers and a dog toilet in the town centre, near the town hall, next to Villa Charles. On ZOU buses, only small dogs under 10 kg are allowed, on your lap or in a basket.</p>
